<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39035" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-sēmĭno</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sow</i> or
				<i>scatter about</i>, <i>to sow</i>
			(rare but class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: ostreas, Cic. Fragm. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 216, 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tamquam ex draconis alicujus dentibus
					proseminati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 6, 10, 19</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to disseminate</i>,
				<i>propagate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proseminatae sunt familiae, i. e. ortae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					de Or. 3, 16, 61</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id.
				Imp. Pomp. 1, 90</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
